;; ⭐ Stone 255.12 THE ADVERSARIAL ROW — a divergence `type_denotation` DOES
;; collapse, which must STILL be refused.
;;
;; `:wat::type::Infer` is a MARKER, not a `wat.type` member: there is no
;; `:wat::core::Infer`, and a field declared with it is `UnknownNamedType` on its
;; own. `edn::render::type_denotation` is a blind prefix rewrite and collapses it
;; regardless — so the first draft of 255.12's cure called these two declarations
;; equivalent, silently SWALLOWED the second (illegal) one as a benign no-op, and
;; this file checked CLEAN. Measured, not reviewed.
;;
;; The cure is `types::denoted_type_path`, which carries the same `Infer`
;; carve-out `check::format_type_path` had already written down in a RENDERER —
;; and which every other consumer of `type_denotation` was missing.
;;
;; ⛔ If this file ever starts freezing OK, the identity door has been widened
;; past what the substrate itself says the `Infer` marker means.
(:wat::core::defrecord :p255_12::Inf [n <- :wat::type::Infer])
(:wat::core::defrecord :p255_12::Inf [n <- :wat::core::Infer])
